wb-node-red (1.0.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: `apt install wb-node-red` runs Node-RED natively on the
    Wiren Board controller.
    - Node-RED + WB palette (node-red-contrib-wirenboard) vendored at build time;
      Node.js from the distro (Depends: nodejs);
    - dedicated unprivileged, hardened systemd service; editor on loopback (1880);
    - reverse-proxied on a dedicated HTTPS port (21880) behind the homeui login
      (admin only); old /node-red/ kept as a redirect; unauth browsers -> login,
      API/CLI -> 401;
    - gate reuses the wb-mqtt-homeui (>= 2.235.4) service-gate snippets and adds a
      per-session /auth/check cache (mutations bypass it) for the editor's burst;
    - default flow wired to localhost:1883 and /devices/#;
    - homeui "Node-RED" menu entry (homeui >= 2.235.4);
    - user data + runtime under /mnt/data; excluded from unattended-upgrades;
    - CycloneDX SBOM shipped (EU CRA).
    Note: reachable on the LAN, not via the WB Cloud tunnel (forwards only 443).

 -- Denis Smagin <denis.smagin@wirenboard.com>  Fri, 26 Jun 2026 20:00:00 +0200
